---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../../components/Arrow.astro';
import DisclosureIcon from '../../../components/DisclosureIcon.astro';
import MediaPlayer from '../../../components/MediaPlayer.astro';
import {nevermore, hasMedia, url, media} from '../../../lib/catalogue';
const release = nevermore.candidate!;
const megabytes = Math.round(nevermore.download!.bytes / 1024 / 1024);
const modes=[
  {name:'SOFT', kicker:'Magical Halloween', text:'Playful, a little spooky and full of surprises. Meet the Midnight Host, take your chances with Trick or Treat, and let ravens, ghosts and small wonders find you.'},
  {name:'HAUNTED', kicker:'Supernatural horror', text:'For when you want the lights off. A darker, cinematic night with rarer encounters that answer your choices. Some things are best left unseen until they find you.'},
];
const moments=[
  {image:'host.webp', title:'Meet the Midnight Host.', text:'A figure emerges. A hand invites you closer. “Trick or Treat?” Your choice matters. What happens next is still a surprise.',alt:'The Skull Warden, Nevermore’s Midnight Host, extends an open hand.'},
  {image:'raven.webp', title:'Something heard you.', text:'Say “Raven” and see what answers. A sweep, a watchful perch, perhaps something closer. The same word never quite brings the same encounter.',alt:'Azure Night raven in flight with detailed charcoal and cool-blue feathers.'},
  {image:'bride.webp', title:'Not everything is a scare.', text:'A spectral bride releases a butterfly. A chest offers a treat. Between the unsettling moments, there is room for something beautiful.',alt:'The Veiled Wraith Bride releases a butterfly from her open palm.'},
];
---
<Layout title="Nevermore — Halloween for AR Smart Glasses | GlassPlay" description="Nevermore is a Halloween haunting with two moods: playful SOFT magic or HAUNTED supernatural horror. Meet the Midnight Host, call the raven, and download it free for Windows." path="experiences/nevermore/" theme="nevermore" social={hasMedia ? 'media/nevermore/glassplay-social.webp' : 'brand/nevermore-social.png'}>
  <section class="nevermore-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="nevermore-title">
    <a class="back-link" href={url('#experiences')}><span class="back-arrow"><Arrow /></span>GlassPlay experiences</a>
    <div class="nevermore-title"><h1 id="nevermore-title">{nevermore.name}</h1><span>{nevermore.theme} · Free download</span></div>
    <div class:list={['nevermore-hero-frame', {'title-art-frame':!hasMedia}]}>
      <img src={hasMedia ? media('cover.webp') : url('brand/nevermore-poster.webp')} srcset={hasMedia ? `${media('cover-small.webp')} 640w, ${media('cover.webp')} 1200w` : `${url('brand/nevermore-poster-small.webp')} 800w, ${url('brand/nevermore-poster.webp')} 1600w`} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 95vw, 90vw" alt={hasMedia ? 'Azure Night raven sweeps into the foreground, with the Midnight Host and Spectral Bride emerging behind it.' : 'Original 3D title artwork: a dark feather with restrained blue highlights.'} width={hasMedia ? '1200' : '1600'} height={hasMedia ? '630' : '1000'} fetchpriority="high" />
      <div class="hero-statement"><p>You armed something.<br /><em>Now it's here.</em></p><a class="button pale" href="#film">Watch the teaser<Arrow /></a><a class="hero-get" href="#get-nevermore">Download free</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="film-section wrap" id="film" aria-labelledby="film-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="film-heading">A glimpse<br /><em>after dark.</em></h2><p>{hasMedia ? 'Turn the sound on. A first look at the encounters waiting inside Nevermore.' : 'Discover the atmosphere and the encounters.'}</p></div>
    <MediaPlayer />
    {hasMedia && <details class="film-description"><summary>Read the film description<DisclosureIcon /></summary><p>The Azure Night raven flies close. The Midnight Host emerges from the dark, inviting a choice with “Trick or Treat?” A Mimic Chest opens, and the Spectral Bride releases a butterfly. Some scenes show the encounters floating over a simulated kitchen. Cloth, wing sounds and the raven’s call accompany the action. This is a short teaser of a few encounters, recorded in Raven Simulator rather than on physical glasses.</p><a href={media('transcript.md')}>Read the complete transcript</a></details>}
  </section>

  <section class="story-intro wrap">
    <h2>Silence.<br />Presence.<br /><em>Then, an encounter.</em></h2>
    <div><p class="large-copy">Halloween isn't waiting on a screen.<br />It's waiting in your field of view.</p><p>Start Nevermore and go on looking at your world. A pair of eyes. A shadow. A raven passing too close. Encounters arrive with space between them, so anticipation has time to grow.</p><p>Some ask you to choose. Some simply arrive. You decide when it all ends.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="modes-section wrap" id="modes" aria-labelledby="modes-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="modes-heading">Two doors.<br /><em>Choose your night.</em></h2><p>Every night begins at two doors. Look at one, or simply click it, and step through. Come back out whenever you like.</p></div>
    <div class="modes">{modes.map(mode=><article><h3>{mode.name}<span class="small-label">{mode.kicker}</span></h3><p>{mode.text}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="moments wrap" aria-label="Nevermore encounters">
    {moments.map((moment,index)=><article class:list={['moment',{'reverse':index%2===1}]}>
      {hasMedia ? <img src={media(moment.image)} srcset={`${media(moment.image.replace('.webp','-small.webp'))} 480w, ${media(moment.image)} 960w`} sizes="(max-width:760px) 90vw, 50vw" alt={moment.alt} width="960" height="720" loading="lazy" /> : <div class:list={['moment-title-art',`moment-art-${index}`]} aria-hidden="true"><span>{index===0 ? 'Trick\nor Treat?' : index===1 ? '“Raven.”' : 'A strange\nkind of beautiful.'}</span></div>}
      <div><h2>{moment.title}</h2><p>{moment.text}</p></div>
    </article>)}
  </section>

  <section class="ritual-section wrap" aria-labelledby="ritual-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="ritual-heading">An invitation.<br /><em>Never an obligation.</em></h2><p>No constant attention required. Nevermore leaves room for the real world, and always leaves you in control.</p></div>
    <ol class="ritual">
      <li><span class="ritual-number">1</span><h3>Choose a door.</h3><p>Soft or haunted. Nothing starts until you step through.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">2</span><h3>Trick or Treat?</h3><p>Meet the Host, make your choice, and see what follows.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">3</span><h3>Call the raven.</h3><p>Say “Raven” and something may answer.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">4</span><h3>Stop any time.</h3><p>Everything goes quiet the moment you say so. Your world is yours again.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="privacy-note"><h3>A haunting that stays with you.</h3><p>Everything runs on your own computer. Nevermore only listens while it is waiting for you, never keeps recordings, and saves your discoveries on your device.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="availability wrap" id="get-nevermore" aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
    <div><h2 id="availability-heading">Your first encounter<br /><em>is waiting.</em></h2><p>Nevermore is free, with both doors included. Play it today on a Windows PC with Raven Simulator.</p><a class="button" href={nevermore.install_url!}>Download for Windows<Arrow /></a><p class="small-copy download-note">Free · about {megabytes} MB · Version {release.version} · <a href={nevermore.release_url!}>Release notes</a></p><a class="text-link creator-link" href="https://github.com/RBraga01">Meet the creator <Arrow /></a></div>
    <div class="compatibility"><h3>Where it runs</h3><dl>{nevermore.targets.map(target=><div><dt>{target.name}</dt><dd>{target.label}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="small-copy">Nevermore needs Raven Framework, which you get separately from Raven.</p></div>
    <div class="technical-details">
      <details><summary>How to install<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>You will need a Windows PC with Python 3.10 or later and Raven Framework 1.0.6, obtained from Raven under its own terms. Raven Framework is not included in the download.</p><ol class="install-steps"><li>Download and extract the ZIP.</li><li>Open PowerShell in the <code>Nevermore-Halloween</code> folder and create an environment: <code>python -m venv .venv</code>, then <code>.venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1</code>.</li><li>Install your copy of Raven Framework into that environment.</li><li>Run <code>python -m pip install -r requirements.txt</code>, then <code>python main.py</code>.</li></ol><p>The download includes a full guide in <code>README.md</code>. The <a href={nevermore.release_url!}>release page</a> has the checksum for verifying your download.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Comfort & good to know<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore has sudden appearances, spiders and close creature encounters. Play it when you choose, at a comfortable volume, and stop whenever you wish. Avoid using it where a distraction could be unsafe.</p><p>On glasses, dark scenes are easiest to see away from very bright surroundings. Voice recognition depends on your microphone and surroundings, and the on-screen controls always work too.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Credits & licensing<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore brings together character artwork created with Meshy, animation made for the experience, recorded sound effects and generated character voices.</p><p>Nevermore’s code is MIT-licensed; its artwork and media are All Rights Reserved. Third-party credits and licenses are included in the download.</p><a href={url('credits/#nevermore')}>Read credits and release information</a></div></details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
